 ],
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.3,
   "text": "Your tap still runs when the power dies.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 2.74,
   "end": 5.49,
   "text": "But why does it stop after about twenty-four hours...",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 5.75,
   "end": 7.01,
   "text": "and what do you lose first?",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 7.49,
   "end": 8.83,
   "text": "This is a what-if.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.1,
   "end": 10.94,
   "text": "Most blackouts end in hours.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.22,
   "end": 12.2,
   "text": "This one doesn't.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 12.44,
   "end": 14.46,
   "text": "We're going to follow it for seven days...",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 14.66,
   "end": 15.7,
   "text": "hour by hour...",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 15.86,
   "end": 19.25,
   "text": "using the rules from the CDC, FEMA and the USDA.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 19.52,
   "end": 20.44,
   "text": "And stay to the end.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.66,
   "end": 23.48,
   "text": "Because the most dangerous moment isn't when the lights go out.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 23.72,
   "end": 24.94,
   "text": "It's when they come back on...",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 25.25,
   "end": 26.75,
   "text": "and you open the fridge.",
   "block": "b00"
  },
  {
   "start": 27.1,
   "end": 29.29,
   "text": "Hour one. Your lights go out.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 29.71,
   "end": 31.25,
   "text": "That's the part everyone expects.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 31.7,
   "end": 32.62,
   "text": "What comes next...",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 32.84,
   "end": 33.99,
   "text": "is what nobody does.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 34.52,
   "end": 35.8,
   "text": "Your card stops working.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 36.26,
   "end": 38.99,
   "text": "Card readers and ATMs need power and a network.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 39.21,
   "end": 40.48,
   "text": "So it's cash only.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 40.96,
   "end": 42.17,
   "text": "Then the gas station.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.6,
   "end": 44.2,
   "text": "Here's the part that surprises people.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 44.6,
   "end": 46.16,
   "text": "The station isn't out of gas.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 46.42,
   "end": 47.95,
   "text": "The tanks under the ground are full.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.33,
   "end": 51.83,
   "text": "But the only thing that lifts that fuel to your car is an electric pump.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 52.27,
   "end": 52.87,
   "text": "No power... no pump.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 53.22,
   "end": 53.75,
   "text": "A few states plan for this.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.28,
   "end": 61.55,
   "text": "Florida, for example, requires many stations near highways and evacuation routes to be wired for a generator.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 61.96,
   "end": 63.91,
   "text": "Most of the country has no rule like that.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 64.45,
   "end": 65.12,
   "text": "And your fridge?",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.48,
   "end": 66.73,
   "text": "It starts a countdown.",
   "block": "b01"
  },
  {
   "start": 67.08,
   "end": 70.66,
   "text": "Hour six. Your fridge just passed its four-hour mark.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 70.95,
   "end": 75.51,
   "text": "The USDA rule: food in a closed fridge stays safe for about four hours.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 75.74,
   "end": 79.38,
   "text": "After that, meat, milk, eggs and leftovers have to go.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 79.66,
   "end": 81.4,
   "text": "Your freezer is your best friend now.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 81.67,
   "end": 83.85,
   "text": "A full one holds for about forty-eight hours.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 84.06,
   "end": 84.55,
   "text": "Half full? Just twenty-four.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 84.82,
   "end": 85.64,
   "text": "Every traffic light is dark.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 86.3,
   "end": 89.86,
   "text": "Many states write it into law: a dead signal means an all-way stop.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 90.09,
   "end": 92.22,
   "text": "And your phone still has signal...",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 92.52,
   "end": 94.82,
   "text": "for now. Here's why that won't last.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 95.14,
   "end": 96.42,
   "text": "A cell tower looks like a pole.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 96.71,
   "end": 98.26,
   "text": "It's really a small building...",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 98.59,
   "end": 102.09,
   "text": "with a room full of batteries at the bottom.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 102.41,
   "end": 107.06,
   "text": "Industry guidelines have called for as little as four hours of backup, with eight as the goal.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 107.32,
   "end": 111.82,
   "text": "After Hurricane Katrina, the FCC tried to require eight hours nationwide.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 112.05,
   "end": 113.45,
   "text": "That rule never took effect.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 113.69,
   "end": 115.39,
   "text": "So the towers are draining.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 115.67,
   "end": 117.75,
   "text": "And so is something you can't see.",
   "block": "b02"
  },
  {
   "start": 118.1,
   "end": 121.1,
   "text": "Hour twelve. Your phone is at forty percent...",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 121.44,
   "end": 122.7,
   "text": "and it's dropping fast.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 123.1,
   "end": 125.57,
   "text": "Your Wi-Fi router died the moment the power did.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 125.87,
   "end": 127.75,
   "text": "So your phone leans on the cell network.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 128.08,
   "end": 129.54,
   "text": "But the towers are weaker now.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 129.91,
   "end": 133.78,
   "text": "As the signal drops, your phone works harder to stay connected...",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 133.94,
   "end": 135.11,
   "text": "and that burns battery.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 135.29,
   "end": 136.8,
   "text": "And everyone is calling at once.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 137.08,
   "end": 138.22,
   "text": "The network jams.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 138.69,
   "end": 142.24,
   "text": "The FCC's advice: keep calls short, and text instead.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 142.54,
   "end": 144.63,
   "text": "A text can get through when a call can't.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 145.01,
   "end": 146.6,
   "text": "You can charge your phone in your car.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.82,
   "end": 149.26,
   "text": "But only with the car outside, in the open.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 149.47,
   "end": 150.63,
   "text": "Never in the garage.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 151.0,
   "end": 151.68,
   "text": "Hold that thought...",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 151.97,
   "end": 153.16,
   "text": "it matters on day two.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 153.49,
   "end": 154.85,
   "text": "But by hour twenty-four...",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 155.04,
   "end": 156.34,
   "text": "the problem isn't your phone.",
   "block": "b03"
  },
  {
   "start": 156.64,
   "end": 157.73,
   "text": "It's your water.",
   "block": "b03"
  }
 ],
 "duration": 158.08
}